A||||23||Ferrari_cdn||People thinking driving a standard is HARD!||||10||
Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||11-08-2001||12:23 AM||||I've just had two friends of mine who wanted to drive a standard, but never had the opportunity.  I just let a friend try my 4spd.  He tried it and drove it through a empty gravel road outside the city.  He thought he would be ****ing everything up but after just ONE stall, he got it running and up to 4th gear.  I told him to stop and start over.  Stalled it again, and then got it running, all through 4 gears.  He said it wasn't as hard as it appeared to be!<P>The other friend, same story.  He said it wasn't as hard as it looked like!<P>Now, only if I could get my girlfriend to actually try it.  She said she likes my Fiero but she would love it even MORE if it was an auto, just because THEN she'll be able to drive it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_cdn.JPG">  </A>  <BR>AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||10
Z||000001||fix||11-08-2001||12:33 AM||||95% of the driving I've done in my life has been in cars with manual trannies.  Personally I feel stupid driving an auto because I'm just along for the ride.  I feel like I have more control in a manual which is why the auto tranny in my fiero is getting swapped for a 5 speed.  Just my personal opinion, so don't flame me. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ferrari_cdn||11-08-2001||12:45 AM||||I know what you're saying.  After driving my Fiero, driving in another car that's auto, felt strange.  Didn't feel like I had control of the car.<p>[This message has been edited by Ferrari_cdn (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000003||artherd||11-08-2001||04:20 AM||||AAACK, I CAN'T FIND THE CLUTCH!!!!!<P>WHY THE HELL WON"T IT LET ME SHIFT, HERE COMES THE TURN!<P>Oh wait, it's an automatic...<P>Sports cars have gearboxes, not slushboxes ;0)<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||Screwie||11-08-2001||04:53 AM||||I don't understand anyway why you all have auto trans in the US and Canada. Here in Europe almost everybody drives manual. Other than old ladies, nobody drives auto... When I first drove a car it took me a whole of 1 minute to understand it and I never once stalled it in my first driving lesson. I've only once ever experienced an autotrans really  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero_24||11-08-2001||07:14 AM||||I hate auto's!  I have always driven manual, and I love them.  Other than my 83 Z28 and 87 GT, is the 2nd auto I have owned out of quite a few cars.  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||11-08-2001||07:45 AM||||My Fiero is the first manual I've ever drove.  Didn't take long for me to learn since I already knew how to drive a stick, just had to go through the monkey motions.  It's not really all that hard, once you know how, it's like riding a bike.<P>I prefer to drive manuals since 98% of people who have been abducted by Aliens drove cars with automatic transmissions...<P>Shift Yourself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Pheagey||11-08-2001||08:36 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tigger:<BR><B>My Fiero is the first manual I've ever drove.  Didn't take long for me to learn since I already knew how to drive a stick, just had to go through the monkey motions.  It's not really all that hard, once you know how, it's like riding a bike.<P>I prefer to drive manuals since 98% of people who have been abducted by Aliens drove cars with automatic transmissions...<P>Shift Yourself    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Do if I swap my 5 speed for an auto and add some landing light to my car do you think I have a chance of being abducted?...<P>{edited for spelling]<BR>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed: Status: destiny unknown.<BR>Broken down: 3 times<BR>Broken into: 2  times (w/i 2 days).<BR>Killed: '97 Civic LX Auto,<BR>Killed by: '93 Civic EX 5 speed,<BR>[link]Http://www.LithiumEffects.com/car.html[/link] (B4 vandalism)<p>[This message has been edited by Pheagey (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||CoolBlue87GT||11-08-2001||08:51 AM||||I agree in part,<P>Driving a manual Fiero is great, I love choosing when to shift, and hearing the engine wind out. "Being in control?" Yes I love that feeling.<P>Couldn't imagine driving an auto Fiero, as I've never driven one. - But it's still a Fiero !!  Yea.<P>Now, for the other part.<P>My daily driver is an automatic - a non decrip Ford Coutour. When I first got it, I lived in MD, and had to drive in rush (why called rush?, you don't go fast) hour traffic going into DC.  Over 60 one way miles.<P>The many stop & starts is a real pain, having to shift over hundred times, "ONE WAY"  plain sucked. <P>Many will say, oh I love to shift, but after 20 + years of rush hour driving, you'll change your mind.  - Now, mind you, I'm not talking about Feiro's.<P>Driving the automatic give's me time to adjust the MP3 player, while I'm receving email on my laptop, as I'm watching the GPS screen showing the world going by, while I'm talking on the phone (W/hands free of course), and typing out a message on my two way pager - Oh, did I miss a shift ?  LOL, (just kidding about this last part) LOL<p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000009||Formula||11-08-2001||09:04 AM||||I prefer an auto because if I tried to drag race (legal) with a stick I would stall it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||88CoupeV6||11-08-2001||10:57 AM||||I will never buy an auto. Once you go stick, you never go back  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||7
Z||000011||sdely||11-08-2001||11:28 AM||||Driving a manual is cool because you can get better at it over time.  It is also just plain fun.  There is nothing like rowing through the gears on the windy roads in the summertime.<BR>When I got my first manual it had a bad clutch master cylinder, which made it very hard to learn on, but now I am infinantley grateful that I did.<P>85 GT 3.1 4.10||||reg||1
Z||000012||BN Boomer||11-08-2001||11:54 AM||||I like both types of transmissions. It is undeniably inherently more fun to drive a stick. But an automatic is far more convenient and a better choice if you do much driving in heavy/rush hour traffic. Wearing your knee out to move a few car lengths at a time gets old pretty fast. Starting from a stop on a steep hill with a stick and someone right behind you can be a challenge at times, too, especially if the road is wet. And I have found automatics to be ultimately superior in snow and ice because they transmit power so much smoother.<P>My 85 GT is an automatic because that's the car I was able to find a good deal on. If I were to get another one, it would most likely be an 87-88 GT with a 5 speed as a I personally don't drive in heavy traffic very often and have far better vehicles for the snow and ice.<P>One other reason that I am beginning to appreciate automatics for is their ability to be driven by people with disabilities. I have a 14 year old nephew who suffered a SCI over the summer and will be in a wheelchair for the rest of his life. I can put hand controls in my automatic Fiero so that he can drive it when he gets his learner's permit next year.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Old Lar||11-08-2001||11:55 AM||||I have to agree with CoolBlue.  Driving a stick is fun EXCEPT in stop and go traffic.<BR>Going through (or around) metro areas like Chicago, Boston or DC where the speed goes from 0 to 70 to 0 to 50 to 0 gets real tiring with a manual transmission.  You are not able to leave three car lengths open in front of you or seven cars try to squeeze in to get 2 feet further down the road.  People must take dumb pills to drive like that.<P>I have both a 5 speed and an auto, but once on the highway at continuous cruising speed, no shifting, no problem.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Master_Sushi||11-08-2001||12:31 PM||||I hate autos. If someone dosent know how to drive a stick shift, I don't even think of them as a real drivers(unless they have a disability obviously). I learned how to drive on a stick shift car, thats the best time to learn a standard.<P>I'm sorry but fieros with autos are sooooooooo boring  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif">. The slushbox 3 speed dosen't help much either.<P>Nothings more fun then blasting through all your gears at WOT! Or blasting down through the gears on a hard stop while draging the rear tires down to speed(dont get me started on fwd).||||reg||14
Z||000015||Fformula88||11-08-2001||12:54 PM||||I can see we have a lot of manual fans here!  I too love the speed and control of the 4-spd in my fathers 85 2m6 when I get a chance to drive it, but find my auto Fiero very satisfying too.  I have driven auto's all my life (well, 7 yrs worth of driving) excapt the last ten months since my father got the 4-spd.  Main reason was I didn't know anybody who had a manual.  However, I find it very distracting to drive, probably because I don't have much practice.  I can certainly get thru the gears fine, and find it easier (and more fun!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) to rocket away from dead stops than to ease it off.  That 1-2 shift is an absolute blast!  At the end of the day, however, its still nice to get into my auto and just cruise around without worrying about having to select the gears.<P>For pure performance driving, the manual is definately much more satisfying.  I would love my Fiero to be a manual, and maybe someday it will, but it was what I found when I was shopping and I love it just the same!||||reg||1
Z||000016||BlackStang95||11-08-2001||01:22 PM||||Most cars I've ever driven and ever car I've owned has been stick.  It's not hard to learn and it quickly become 2nd nature.  I think all cars that are supposed to be remotely sporty should only come with manuals but I think all other cars besides trucks should come with autos.  Theres really no need for it.  I read somewhere that 85 percent of americans can't drive a stick....thats crazy.  I also think clutchless manuals and all are stupid and they should pick one of the other.  The only car I would want an auto in is if I was rich and got me a luxury car to chill and floss with....im thinking navigator  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.  But other than that manual all the way.  ||||reg||10
Z||000017||Ferrari_cdn||11-08-2001||01:37 PM||||I agree with the rest of you guys!  But any of you got a problem with girlfriends or boyfriends who once in a while complain about not being able to drive it?||||reg||10
Z||000018||rogergarrison||11-08-2001||01:38 PM||||I agree with lar. Ya its fun driving out in the country with a stick. But for those 2 mile long, bumper to bumper traffic jams and around town, Id have to have an auto. My next project/kit, whatever it ends up being will def be an auto. I wouldnt care if its a LT1 in a Lambo, it gotta be auto. You gotta realize too that autos have come a long way since the 80's. In most cases, there faster and far more reliable than sticks. Most people are abusive to clutches too, like holding them in with car in gear at a stop lite. I see a lot of people in here replacing them over n over at 50k or so. If you know how to drive a stick properly, a clutch should last as long as the car. I know people with 30's model cars still with originals. So anyway back to it, i like sticks for over the road OK, autos for in town.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||CoolBlue87GT||11-08-2001||02:15 PM||||Hey, there's another thing that's cool about a manual ...<P>Down shifting !!  I love that to.  Coming to a light, downshift to slow down, and hearing the exhaust sound "bark". <P>I changed my earlier post, a Fiero w/ auto is still a Fiero !! Didn't want to seem as if I was flaming owners with automatic's.||||reg||6
Z||000020||BN Boomer||11-08-2001||02:22 PM||||Psssssst..... (whisper) Hey buddy, didya' know that if you push in the button on left side of the automatic shifter and pull the shifter back a notch or two you are downshifting as well? (/whisper)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||rogergarrison||11-08-2001||07:04 PM||||I thought the same thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I prefer not to downshift just coming up to lites and stop signs. Its just more wear and tear on clutch (see above) brake pads are way cheaper than clutch kits.||||reg||1
Z||000022||formula2||11-08-2001||07:14 PM||||My first standard is my Fiero and i would not buy an auto fiero.....<BR>But i appreciate the auto in my Savana while in heavy traffic, going to work..<BR>I love to shift, but on week ends only..||||reg||1
Z||000023||Back On Holiday||11-08-2001||09:10 PM||||I must say, I drive a UPS truck, and while I drive stick all day, driving the fiero home is a treat.  <P>also, a side note...this week I've been covering for another driver who has one of the BRAND NEW auto-shift trucks, and that thing is NICE.  it MOVES Faster than you can shift.  anyway, when I'm done and get into the Fiero, it's nice to feel the clutch pedal  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
